ects in cervical carcinomas limit the presentation of a CTL epitope from human papillomavirus 16 E6.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>167</volume><fpage>5420</fpage><lpage>5428</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11673561</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003097-Agrawal1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Agrawal</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Reemtsma</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bagiella</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Oluwole</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Braunstein</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Role of TAP-1 and/or TAP-2 antigen presentation defects in tumorigenicity of mouse melanoma.</article-title><source>Cell Immunol</source><volume>228</volume><fpage>130</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15219464</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003097-Zhang1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>QJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Seipp</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Vitalis</surname><given-names>TZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>XL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>TAP expression reduces IL-10 expressing tumor infiltrating lymphocytes and restores immunosurveillance against melanoma.</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003097-Huang1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name><name><surname>Golumbek</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmadzadeh</sur